@node dynamic-eq Plugin Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

Dynamic EQ — frequency-selective dynamics processing.

@subsubheading What It Does

A parametric EQ where each filter band only activates when the signal in that frequency range crosses a threshold. Unlike a static EQ that applies constant gain, a dynamic EQ adapts in real-time — useful for taming resonances that only appear at certain levels or for frequency-dependent compression.

@subsubheading Features

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Per-band dynamics}: Each EQ band has its own threshold, ratio, attack, and release
@item @strong{Parametric EQ base}: Standard frequency, Q, and gain per band
@item @strong{Adaptive processing}: Gain changes dynamically based on signal level
@end itemize


